2026-08-10T03:33:06Z FOLLOW-UP: "Automation jobs" was reading "no GitHub token" on the live panel. Cause: launchd runs a STANDALONE COPY at ~/.stowaway-ops/publish_health.py (ops/com.stowaway.healthpublish.plist line 14), not ops/publish_health.py in the repo. The snapshot's CHECKS come from a fresh main-pinned clone so a new check goes live at once, but a change to publish_health.py does not land until someone copies the file across by hand - so the GH_TOKEN hand-off I added would never have run, and the check would have sat at "unknown" forever while looking installed. health_monitor now falls back to reading the PAT from the mounted tree's .secrets itself. Worth remembering generally: ops/*.py in this repo is not necessarily what the Mac executes.
