2026-08-15T03:14:48Z   MONDAY MARKETING - PREVIOUS RUN'S READING WAS WRONG, AND ZAK CALLED IT. This log entry exists to correct it before it hardens into folklore. Earlier today this analysis reported that mari 'burns A$165.37 of Uber Ads on Mondays she is closed, 5 Mondays out of 5, ~A$1,720/yr of pure waste'. Zak's challenge: isn't the Monday charge just the WHOLE PREVIOUS WEEK's ad spend, settled on the Monday? The evidence says he is right and the waste framing was an unfounded leap - the payout Marketing line tells you WHEN Uber deducted money, not WHAT PERIOD it covers, and that distinction was skipped.
2026-08-15T03:14:48Z   EVIDENCE FOR THE WEEKLY-ROLLUP READING: (1) The five Monday charges are 37.47, 29.10, 32.59, 30.75, 35.46 - mean A$33.07, stdev A$3.05, a 9% coefficient of variation. Per-click ad spend on a day with zero orders would be near zero or wildly erratic; a stable ~A$33 weekly figure is exactly what a small ongoing daily budget (~A$4.70/day) bills out to. (2) Each charge tracks the sales of the week that ENDED THE DAY BEFORE, at a tight and rising ratio: 0.63%, 0.69%, 0.82%, 0.83%. A same-day charge on a closed day should track nothing. (3) The Monday always falls the day after a Mon-Sun week closes - the same Mon-Sun weeks Uber uses on its own invoices, e.g. "Uber to shop (Week of 08/03-08/09)". (4) Trading-day marketing runs 11.10% of sales with a per-day stdev of 7.7pp and is non-zero on 27 of 28 trading days - that is funded-offer behaviour scaling with orders, a different animal from the flat Monday line. (5) 2026-07-13 is the FIRST row in the feed and already carries a Monday charge, i.e. for a week that predates the feed entirely.
2026-08-15T03:14:48Z   WHAT WOULD MAKE IT PROOF, AND WHY IT IS NOT YET: no ads REPORTING view was found in the portal. The 'Ads' nav item leads to /manager/marketing/create/ads, a campaign CREATION flow, not a spend history - and note it loaded showing "Harry Gatos" despite an explicit mari restaurantUUID in the URL, the sticky selector again, on a page with a live "Create ad" button. Nothing was created. The Offers page likewise shows only recommendations, no active-campaign list. The decisive artifact would be a weekly "Uber to shop" invoice PDF itemising ad spend with its billing period - downloading one needs Zak's go-ahead and was not done. Until then this is strong circumstantial evidence, not proof.
2026-08-15T03:14:48Z   CONSEQUENCE IF THE ROLLUP READING IS RIGHT: the A$165.37 is real spend and NOT waste - it buys clicks across the whole preceding week, including the busy Fri/Sat. But dating it to the Monday it was deducted slightly MISDATES marketing cost at day level: Monday carries a week's ad cost against zero revenue, and the week that consumed the ads carries none. It washes out at weekly and monthly grain, which is where the P&L reads it, so nothing is being overstated in aggregate. NO CHANGE MADE - the runbook is explicit that portal figures go in by the date the portal reports them, and inventing an accrual here would break the per-day payout identity that every guard depends on. Flagged only so nobody reads a Monday day-level P&L as a bad trading day.
2026-08-15T03:14:48Z   STILL WORTH A LOOK, ON ITS OWN MERITS: mari marketing is 11.9% of sales across the feed (A$2,329) ON TOP of 25.2% commission, so roughly 37c in the dollar goes to Uber before COGS. hg by contrast runs ZERO marketing at 31.8% commission. And the Monday ad charge as a share of the prior week's sales has risen every single week measured - 0.63 to 0.69 to 0.82 to 0.83% - a small number moving consistently in one direction. Neither is an error; both are Zak's discretionary call, which is the whole reason marketing is kept split out from commission in this feed.
